# "# en:" shows the English source. [hash] marks the English version a line was translated from;
# lines marked STALE need updating — after fixing the text, delete the [hash] and re-run the tool.


@event shop_country_market
# en: The Country Market
title [7dc8ba] = 乡间集市
# en: {~Behind the market cross, away from the green's stalls, is the row the valley actually shops at: a crook-maker splitting ash, a cloak-seller under a rack of waxed cloaks, the bee-woman in her veil with her combs, and a girl turning oatcakes on a griddle.|The back row again. The crook-maker is arguing with a shepherd about an inch of handle, the cloak-seller is asleep standing up, and the bee-woman has a bee on her nose and doesn't care.}
text [9a89b0] = {~市集十字架后面，离开草地上的那些摊子，才是山谷里的人真正买东西的那一排：做牧羊杖的人在劈白蜡木，卖斗篷的站在一排打蜡斗篷下面，养蜂女人戴着面纱守着她的蜂巢，还有个姑娘在铁鏊上翻燕麦饼。|又是后排。做牧羊杖的人正跟一个牧羊人为杖柄的一寸长短争个不休，卖斗篷的站着睡着了，养蜂女人鼻子上停着一只蜜蜂，她毫不在意。}
# en: The back row of a village market under a stone market cross, a crook-maker splitting ash, a cloak-seller among hanging waxed cloaks, a bee-woman with combs under a veil, a girl at an oatcake griddle, a student browsing.
scene [d76342] = 石砌市集十字架下乡村集市的后排，一个做牧羊杖的人在劈白蜡木，一个卖斗篷的站在挂着的打蜡斗篷间，一个戴面纱的养蜂女人守着蜂巢，一个姑娘守着燕麦饼铁鏊，一个学生在逛。
# en: A comb of heather honey
opt.honey.label [ab5c00] = 一块石楠蜜
# en: Health and Mood.
opt.honey.hint [f489c1] = 健康和心情。
# en: {~The bee-woman cuts you a square of dark comb and wraps it in a dock leaf, for a coin. You eat it on the steps of the cross, wax and all.|The bee-woman takes your coin and lifts her veil to look at you before she sells. "You'll want the bitter one," she says. She's right.}
opt.honey.say.1 [33731c] = {~养蜂女人收了你一枚硬币，切给你一方深色的蜂巢，用一片酸模叶包着。你坐在十字架的台阶上连蜡带蜜吃了个精光。|养蜂女人收下你的硬币，卖之前掀起面纱打量了你一眼。“你要苦的那种，”她说。她说对了。}
# en: Oatcakes off the griddle
opt.oatcakes.label [e558d5] = 刚出鏊的燕麦饼
# en: Health; it ends a hungry month.
opt.oatcakes.hint [f3d661] = 生命；能结束一个挨饿的月份。
# en: {~A coin buys a stack of oatcakes hot off the griddle, with a knob of butter melting through. The girl turns the next batch with her fingers and doesn't burn them.|The oatcake girl takes your coin and gives you the broken ones too, free. "They taste the same," she says. They taste better.}
opt.oatcakes.say.1 [cad88d] = {~一枚硬币买一摞刚出鏊的燕麦饼，上面一块黄油正化开。那姑娘用手指翻下一锅，居然不烫手。|卖燕麦饼的姑娘收了你的硬币，又把碎了的那些白送给你。“味道一样，”她说。其实更好吃。}
# en: A waxed cloak for the upland
opt.cloak.label [bff8b7] = 一件高地穿的打蜡斗篷
# en: A robe for fights: more Health, and beasts' blows hurt you less.
opt.cloak.hint [ecbaeb] = 战斗用长袍：更多生命，野兽伤你更轻。
# en: {~You count out the coins for heavy waxed wool that smells of sheep and rain. The cloak-seller swears a man once slept a winter night on the ridge in it and woke up warm. He might have been the man.|The cloak-seller wakes up long enough to take your money. You put it on and the wind off the moor gives up trying.}
opt.cloak.say.1 [5b191a] = {~你数出钱，买下厚重的打蜡羊毛，闻起来是羊和雨的味道。卖斗篷的发誓说有人穿着它在山脊上睡了一个冬夜，醒来时暖暖和和。那人说不定就是他自己。|卖斗篷的醒了一会儿，刚好够他收你的钱。你一穿上，荒原上的风就放弃了。}
# en: A shepherd's crook
opt.crook.label [8e7d4d] = 一根牧羊杖
# en: A crook of seasoned ash: on the moors, one fall more you can survive.
opt.crook.hint [d8cc30] = 一根风干的白蜡木牧羊杖：在荒原上，你能多挺过一次跌倒。
# en: {~You pay, and the crook-maker hands you one of seasoned ash with a horn handle. "For the bog roads," he says. "Feel ahead with it. The moor tells you where it's soft, if you ask with a stick."|He takes your coins, weighs you up and chooses a crook to match your height, then cuts an inch off it. "You'll stoop on the moor," he says. "Everybody does."}
opt.crook.say.1 [62c229] = {~你付了钱，做牧羊杖的人递给你一根风干白蜡木、牛角柄的牧羊杖。“走沼泽路用的，”他说，“拿它探着走。你用棍子问，荒原就会告诉你哪儿是软的。”|他收了你的钱，打量着你，挑了一根和你一样高的，又锯掉一寸。“在荒原上你会弯着腰，”他说，“人人都这样。”}
# en: Watch the crook-maker work
opt.look.label [6cffa7] = 看做牧羊杖的人干活
# en: {~You watch the crook-maker steam an ash pole and bend its head round a form, slow as a clock hand. He doesn't speak, and you don't, and it's the most restful half hour of your break.|The shepherd and the crook-maker settle their inch at last. Neither of them is happy. They shake on it.}
opt.look.say.1 [4348c5] = {~你看着做牧羊杖的人把一根白蜡木杆蒸软，绕着模子把杖头弯过来，慢得像钟表的指针。他不说话，你也不说，这是你整个假期里最安宁的半个钟头。|牧羊人和做牧羊杖的人终于为那一寸达成了协议。两人都不满意。他们握手成交。}

@event shop_hedge_door
# en: The Hedge-Witch's Door
title [4fea6b] = 乡野女巫的门
# en: {has(origin_hedge): The hedge-witch's half-door, your grandmother's door, open over the reeds as it always is, with the jars on the sill and the rue drying above. Neighbours come up the plank all day for remedies, and pay in eggs, coin or news. "Same price for you," she says. "Family pays double."|The hedge-witch keeps a half-door over the reeds, open for anyone who comes up the plank, with jars on the sill and bunches of rue drying under the eaves. She sells remedies to the valley for coin, eggs or news, and serves a stranger without once meeting their eye.}
text [1901b7] = {has(origin_hedge): 乡野女巫的半截门——你祖母的门——一如既往地朝芦苇开着，窗台上摆着罐子，芸香在檐下晾着。邻居们整天顺着木板走上来讨药，付鸡蛋、硬币或者消息。“你也是一样的价，”她说，“家里人付双倍。”|乡野女巫在芦苇上方开着一扇半截门，谁顺着木板走上来都行，窗台上摆着罐子，檐下晾着一束束芸香。她给山谷里的人卖药，收硬币、鸡蛋或者消息，招呼外乡人时一眼也不看对方。}
# en: A stilt house at the edge of a reed marsh, bunches of dried herbs hanging under its eaves, a lined old hedge-witch at a half-door with jars on the sill.
scene [0101de] = 芦苇沼泽边的一座高脚屋，檐下挂着一束束晒干的草药，一位满脸皱纹的老乡野女巫站在半截门后，窗台上摆着罐子。
# en: A bunch of rue for your pocket
opt.rue.label [81989b] = 一束放在口袋里的芸香
# en: Rue against the moor: on the moors, one fall more you can survive.
opt.rue.hint [ea9ad3] = 防荒原的芸香：在荒原上，你能多挺过一次跌倒。
# en: She ties the rue with red thread, the way she did when you were small, and puts it in your pocket herself, and takes your penny anyway. "Keep it by you on the high ground," she says. "Don't ask me why. You know why."
opt.rue.say.1 [a1ac9a] = 她像你小时候那样用红线把芸香扎好，亲手放进你的口袋，照样收了你一便士。“上了高地就带在身边，”她说，“别问我为什么。你知道为什么。”
# en: A poultice for what hurts
opt.poultice.label [8ce514] = 一贴止痛的膏药
# en: Health, and it mends an injury.
opt.poultice.hint [eab664] = 健康，还能治好伤。
# en: {~You pay for a poultice of comfrey and something green that smells of the bottom of a pond. It hurts worse for an hour, and then it doesn't hurt at all.|She takes your coin, binds it on herself, briskly, and tells you off for the injury as she does it.}
opt.poultice.say.1 [72cfb2] = {~你付钱买了一贴聚合草和某种闻起来像池塘底的绿东西做的膏药。头一个小时疼得更厉害，然后就一点也不疼了。|她收了你的硬币，亲手给你敷上，手脚麻利，一边敷一边数落你怎么弄伤的。}
# en: A sprig of rosemary that won't wilt
opt.rosemary.label [99f5d6] = 一枝不会枯萎的迷迭香
# en: Health each month for a while.
opt.rosemary.hint [88ea83] = 一段时间内每月恢复生命。
# en: {~She takes your coin, snaps a sprig of rosemary from the pot by the door, breathes on it and gives it to you. "That won't wilt till it's done its work," she says. It doesn't.|A sprig of rosemary on a thread, for a coin. "For the road," she says, "and the road back."}
opt.rosemary.say.1 [79d4d8] = {~她收了你的硬币，从门边的花盆里折下一枝迷迭香，冲它哈了口气，递给你。“它不做完该做的事就不会枯，”她说。它确实没枯。|一枚硬币，换一枝系在线上的迷迭香。“路上带着，”她说，“回来的路上也带着。”}
# en: Just pass the time of day
opt.look.label [f6e707] = 只是聊聊天
# en: {has(origin_hedge): You sit on the step with her for a while and say nothing, which is how you always talked.|You pass the time of day, and she passes it back, and the reeds talk between you.}
opt.look.say.1 [22c491] = {has(origin_hedge): 你和她在台阶上坐了一会儿，什么也没说，你们从来就是这么聊天的。|你跟她打个招呼，她也回个招呼，芦苇在你们之间说着话。}

@event ford_crossing
# en: The Ferryman's Toll
title [d8998f] = 摆渡人的过路费
# en: {&The river's up and the stepping stones are under it. The old ferryman will take you over in his punt, but he doesn't take coin. "Something odd," he says. "A button. A tune. Something you'd miss."|The river's low and the stones are dry, but the ferryman calls from his punt anyway. "Stones are slippery today," he says. "Toll's the same. Something odd."|Mist on the ford, the stones half-hidden. The ferryman holds out his hand without a word. On his wrist, threaded on a string, are a hundred odd tolls: buttons, bird skulls, a key, a tooth.}
text [cd379b] = {&河水涨了，踏脚石淹在水下。老摆渡人愿意用平底船载你过去，但他不收钱。“要件古怪的东西，”他说，“一颗纽扣。一支曲子。你会舍不得的东西。”|河水很浅，踏脚石露在外面，可摆渡人还是从船上叫你。“今天石头滑，”他说，“过路费照旧。古怪的东西。”|渡口起了雾，踏脚石半隐半现。摆渡人一言不发地伸出手。他手腕上用绳子串着上百件古怪的过路费：纽扣、鸟头骨、一把钥匙、一颗牙。}
# en: A wide shallow river ford with stepping stones, an old ferryman sitting by his flat punt on the bank, holding out a weathered hand to a student.
scene [a6a3e6] = 宽阔的浅水渡口，一排踏脚石，老摆渡人坐在岸边的平底船旁，向一个学生伸出饱经风霜的手。
# en: Pay his odd toll
opt.left.label [fa9165] = 付他古怪的过路费
# en: {&You give him a button off your coat. He threads it on his string with a hundred others and poles you over, and when you look back he's sitting on the far bank again, which is the side you started from.|You hum him a tune you made up as a child. He listens carefully, nods and poles you over humming it. You can't remember it afterwards. It's gone.|You give him a hair ribbon you were fond of. He takes it gravely, ties it on, and the punt crosses through the mist without a sound.}
opt.left.say.1 [ca23e8] = {&你从外套上扯下一颗纽扣给他。他把它和其他上百颗串在一起，撑船送你过去，等你回头看时，他又坐在了对岸——也就是你出发的那一边。|你哼了一支小时候自己编的曲子给他听。他认真听完，点点头，一边哼着它一边撑船送你过去。事后你怎么也想不起那支曲子了。它没了。|你给了他一条你很喜欢的发带。他郑重地收下系好，平底船悄无声息地穿过了雾。}
# en: Cross on the stones
opt.right.label [28967b] = 踩着石头过河
# en: {&You go over the drowned stones by feel, knee-deep, cold to the bone and laughing. The ferryman watches you all the way and looks, if anything, disappointed.|Stone to stone, quick and dry-shod. The ferryman claps, slowly, from his punt.|You cross in the mist by counting stones: nine. Coming back at dusk, you count them again: eight. You don't think about it.}
opt.right.say.1 [09b3f5] = {&你凭感觉踩着淹在水下的石头过去，水没到膝盖，冷到骨头里，你却笑着。摆渡人一路看着你，看上去反倒有点失望。|一块接一块，又快又干地过了河。摆渡人在船上慢慢地鼓掌。|你在雾里数着石头过河：九块。黄昏回来时你又数了一遍：八块。你不去想这件事。}
# en: {&The third stone rolls and you go in to the waist. The river is very cold and very interested in your boots. The ferryman fishes you out with his pole, and doesn't charge.|You slip on the slick stone and sit down hard in the shallows. The ferryman doesn't laugh, which is worse.|In the mist you miss a stone entirely and go in to the chest. You come out shaking, on the bank you started from.}
opt.right.say.2 [99dcd1] = {&第三块石头一滚，你掉进水里，水没到腰。河水冰冷，对你的靴子很感兴趣。摆渡人用篙把你捞上来，没收钱。|你在滑溜溜的石头上一滑，重重地坐进浅水里。摆渡人没笑，这更糟。|在雾里你整整踩空了一块石头，水没到胸口。你哆嗦着爬上来，还是在你出发的那一岸。}

@event ford_spate_cart
# en: The River in Spate
title [ce4c7c] = 涨水的河
# en: After a night of rain on the upland the ford is in spate, brown and fast, and a carter has tried it anyway. His cart is stuck mid-stream, the water's up to the axles and rising, and the horse is panicking in the traces. The carter's on the bank, shouting at the horse, the river and you, in that order.
text [7c7537] = 高地下了一夜雨，渡口涨了水，浑黄湍急，可一个赶车人还是硬闯了。他的车卡在河中央，水已经没到车轴还在涨，马在挽具里惊慌失措。赶车人在岸上大喊，依次冲着马、河和你。
# en: A river ford in brown flood, a farm cart stuck mid-stream with its horse panicking in the traces, a farmer on the bank shouting, a student wading in.
scene [4816b5] = 涨满浑黄洪水的渡口，一辆农家马车卡在河中央，马在挽具里惊慌挣扎，岸上的农夫在大喊，一个学生正蹚水过去。
# en: Wade in and calm the horse
opt.left.label [50e701] = 蹚过去安抚那匹马
# en: You get to the horse's head with the water at your chest and talk it down, slowly, nose to nose, until it'll walk. Horse, cart and you come out together onto the far bank. The carter gives you a cheese, a whole one, and tells everybody.
opt.left.say.1 [2708c8] = 你在没到胸口的水里走到马头前，鼻子对鼻子，慢慢地跟它说话，直到它肯走。马、车和你一起上了对岸。赶车人送了你一块奶酪，一整块，还逢人就讲。
# en: The current takes your feet and you go under once, twice, and grab the cart's wheel. The ferryman gets the horse out with his pole and you out with the other end. The cart's lost downriver. So, very nearly, were you.
opt.left.say.2 [d32a9a] = 激流冲走了你的脚，你沉下去一次、两次，抓住了车轮。摆渡人用篙的一头把马拉了出来，用另一头把你拉了出来。车被冲到了下游。你也差点。
# en: Free the traces with a spell
opt.right.label [7ee4c7] = 用咒语割断挽具
# en: You cut the traces from the bank with a snap of your wand, and the horse surges out free. The cart goes off downriver towards the mill with a cargo of turnips. The carter is so glad about the horse he pays you anyway.
opt.right.say.1 [375a9a] = 你在岸上一挥魔杖割断了挽具，马猛地冲了出来。马车载着一车萝卜朝磨坊漂去。赶车人为马高兴得不得了，照样付了你钱。
# en: Your spell cuts the wrong strap, and the cart tips. Horse and carter are fine. The turnips are now the river's. The carter tells you exactly what he thinks of the academy.
opt.right.say.2 [447eb6] = 你的咒语割错了带子，车翻了。马和赶车人都没事。萝卜现在归河了。赶车人原原本本地告诉你他对学院的看法。

@event ford_ferryman_side
# en: Which Side
title [8b1a25] = 哪一边
# en: You've noticed something about the old ferryman: he takes people over and back all day, and he never gets out of the punt, on either side. Not to eat. Not for anything. You ask him, half joking, which bank is his. He looks at you for a long moment, the punt quite still in the current. "Whichever's the other one," he says.
text [378b2c] = 你注意到老摆渡人的一件事：他整天载人来来回回，却从不下船，哪一边都不下。不为吃饭，不为任何事。你半开玩笑地问他哪边才是他的岸。他看了你好一会儿，船在水流里一动不动。“另外那一边，”他说，“不管哪边是另外那一边。”
# en: A quiet river ford at evening, an old ferryman in his punt mid-stream not moving, a student on the bank calling to him.
scene [1fac23] = 傍晚安静的渡口，老摆渡人站在河中央的平底船上一动不动，一个学生在岸上喊他。
# en: Ask him what he means
opt.left.label [aa2647] = 问他是什么意思
# en: He tells you he crossed once, years ago, the wrong way, and it's easier to stay on the water. Then he poles away downstream and doesn't come back for an hour. You've learned something, and you don't know what. You're cold all evening.
opt.left.say.1 [29c074] = 他告诉你，他多年前过过一次河，走错了方向，从那以后待在水上更容易些。然后他撑着船往下游去了，一个小时都没回来。你学到了些什么，却不知道是什么。你冷了一整个傍晚。
# en: Bring him a pie from the market
opt.right.label [99fccd] = 从集市给他带个馅饼
# en: You bring him a hot pie and hand it out to the punt. He eats it on the water, slowly, watching both banks. "Kind," he says. "You're kind. Mind the seventh step on the stones." Then he won't say anything else.
opt.right.say.1 [146a3a] = 你带来一个热馅饼，递到船上。他在水上慢慢吃着，看着两岸。“心好，”他说，“你心好。当心石头上的第七步。”然后他再也不肯多说一句。

@event coppice_rides
# en: Along the Rides
title [fd72fa] = 林间小道
# en: {&Hollin Coppice is all rides and clearings, straight young poles from stumps older than the villages, and the floor of it is a larder if you know where to look.|In the coppice the charcoal burners are cutting this year's panel, and the rides are full of the sound of billhooks and the smell of sap.|The coppice in a soft rain, every leaf dripping, the rides empty except for a woodpecker and you.}
text [15ebef] = {&霍林矮林里到处是小道和空地，笔直的嫩枝从比村子还老的树桩上长出来，要是你知道往哪儿看，林地就是一座储藏室。|矮林里烧炭人正在砍今年的那一片，小道上满是砍刀声和树液的气味。|细雨中的矮林，每片叶子都在滴水，小道上空荡荡的，只有一只啄木鸟和你。}
# en: A sunlit coppice wood of straight young hazel and ash poles growing from old stools, grassy rides between them, a student with a basket among ferns and fungi.
scene [f0a5a9] = 阳光照耀的矮林，笔直的榛树和白蜡嫩枝从老树桩上长出，枝间是长满草的小道，一个学生提着篮子站在蕨草和蘑菇之间。
# en: Forage along the rides
opt.left.label [2bf28e] = 沿着小道采集
# en: {&{season == "winter": Catkins on the hazels, a ring of velvet shank on a dead stool and a patch of something your herbal calls "use with care". You come home scratched to the elbows with a basket worth a week of lessons.|Wood sorrel, the first hazelnuts, a ring of chanterelles and a patch of something your herbal calls "use with care". You come home scratched to the elbows with a basket worth a week of lessons.}|Among the cut stools you find birch polypore and a clump of comfrey the burners don't want. The brambles take their toll on your arms.|Rain brings the mushrooms up. You fill your basket, and your boots fill with water.}
opt.left.say.1 [2f3fbc] = {&{season == "winter": 榛树的葇荑花序、枯树桩上一圈冬菇，还有一丛你的草药书上写着“慎用”的东西。你回家时胳膊一直刮伤到肘，篮子里装着值一星期课的东西。|木酢浆草、头一批榛子、一圈鸡油菌，还有一丛你的草药书上写着“慎用”的东西。你回家时胳膊一直刮伤到肘，篮子里装着值一星期课的东西。}|在砍过的树桩间，你找到了桦木层孔菌，还有一丛烧炭人不要的聚合草。荆棘在你胳膊上收了过路费。|雨把蘑菇催了出来。你装满了篮子，靴子也灌满了水。}
# en: Help the charcoal burners
opt.right.label [d5a45b] = 帮烧炭人干活
# en: {&You stack cordwood for the burners' mound all afternoon, black to the eyebrows. They pay in coin and sausage, and tell you the mound must never be left unwatched, not for a minute, not ever.|You help bundle the cut poles. The burners pay you and sing while they work, a song with seven verses and no chorus. Your shoulders are raw.|The burners need their mound turfed before the rain gets in. You turf it, wet through, and they pay you double for the weather.}
opt.right.say.1 [92c3f1] = {&你给烧炭人的炭堆码了一下午柴，黑到眉毛。他们付了硬币和香肠，还告诉你炭堆绝不能没人看着，一分钟都不行，永远不行。|你帮着捆砍下的枝条。烧炭人付了钱，边干边唱一首有七段没有副歌的歌。你的肩膀磨破了。|下雨前炭堆得盖上草皮。你浑身湿透地把草皮盖好，他们因为天气付了你双倍。}

@event coppice_woodward
# en: The Woodward's Marks
title [2e9ce7] = 林务人的记号
# en: Down a far ride you finally see who chalks the marks on every seventh tree: a tall, stooped man in a green coat so old it's grey, who moves from trunk to trunk with a lump of chalk and doesn't hurry. The burners say nobody hired him and nobody remembers him starting. He sees you, and holds the chalk out.
text [54741b] = 在一条偏远的小道上，你终于看见了每第七棵树上的粉笔记号是谁画的：一个高个子、驼背的男人，穿着一件旧得发灰的绿外套，拿着一块粉笔从一棵树走到另一棵，不慌不忙。烧炭人说没人雇过他，也没人记得他是什么时候开始的。他看见了你，把粉笔递了过来。
# en: A coppice ride with a tall stooped man in an old green coat chalking a mark on a tree trunk, a student watching from behind a stool of hazel.
scene [eac841] = 矮林小道上，一个穿旧绿外套、驼背的高个男人正在树干上画粉笔记号，一个学生躲在一丛榛树桩后看着。
# en: Take the chalk and mark the next one
opt.left.label [bb4f98] = 接过粉笔，标下一棵
# en: You count seven trees and chalk the seventh. He nods, takes the chalk back and walks on into the wood, and you can't see where he goes. All the way home you count things in sevens without meaning to: steps, fence posts, crows.
opt.left.say.1 [21a53c] = 你数了七棵树，在第七棵上画了记号。他点点头，收回粉笔，走进了林子，你看不出他往哪儿去了。回家的一路上，你不由自主地按七来数东西：脚步，篱笆桩，乌鸦。
# en: Ask him who he works for
opt.right.label [876f72] = 问他替谁干活
# en: "The wood," he says, as if it were obvious, and goes on chalking. You ask what the marks are for. "Counting," he says. "Somebody has to." When you look again the ride is empty and the chalk is wet on a tree you'd swear he never reached.
opt.right.say.1 [1a5440] = “林子，”他说，好像这再明显不过，然后继续画。你问记号是做什么用的。“计数，”他说，“总得有人数。”你再看时，小道上空无一人，一棵你发誓他根本没走到的树上，粉笔印还是湿的。

@event coppice_charcoal_night
# en: Watching the Mound
title [126c86] = 守炭堆
# en: A charcoal mound has to be watched all night, every night of the burn, or it flares and the whole charge is ash. The two burners on tonight have a pot on the fire and a spare log to sit on, and they're glad of a third. "Stay and watch," says the older one. "We'll tell you about the wood."
text [f5d410] = 烧炭时，炭堆得整夜有人守着，每一夜都得守，不然它会窜起火来，整窑都烧成灰。今晚守夜的两个烧炭人在火上架着一口锅，还有一根空着的圆木可坐，有第三个人他们很高兴。“留下来守吧，”年长的那个说，“我们给你讲讲这片林子。”
# en: A charcoal burners' camp in a wood clearing at night, a smoking turf-covered mound glowing in the dark, two burners at a small fire inviting a student to sit with them.
scene [da4f7b] = 夜晚林间空地上的烧炭营地，一座盖着草皮的炭堆在黑暗中冒烟发光，两个烧炭人坐在小火堆边招呼一个学生坐下。
# en: Sit up all night with them
opt.left.label [fec50b] = 陪他们守一整夜
# en: You sit up with them till dawn, poking the mound when it smokes wrong, while they tell you about the wood: the stools older than the villages, a winter when the mound went out and nobody spoke of it, the woodward who chalks the trees. You're stiff and smoked like a ham by morning.
opt.left.say.1 [e0403e] = 你陪他们守到天亮，炭堆冒烟不对劲时就捅一捅，听他们讲这片林子：比村子还老的树桩，一个炭堆熄灭了、从此没人再提的冬天，还有那个在树上画粉笔的林务人。到早上你浑身僵硬，被熏得像块火腿。
# en: Share their supper and go
opt.right.label [172e68] = 吃了他们的晚饭就走
# en: You put a coin in for the pot, and they give you rabbit stew and three good stories, and send you home before the dark comes down properly. {at_home(): "Mind the dark on the way," says the older one. "You know the wood. Doesn't mean it knows you."|"Not a place to walk late," says the older one, "for folk who aren't from here."}
opt.right.say.1 [9afeed] = 你往锅里添了一枚硬币，他们给你盛了兔肉汤，讲了三个好故事，在天真正黑下来之前打发你回家。{at_home(): “路上当心天黑，”年长的那个说，“你认得这片林子，可不等于它认得你。”|“不是走夜路的地方，”年长的那个说，“对不是本地的人来说。”}

@event tarn_still_water
# en: The Still Water
title [899a25] = 静水
# en: {&The tarn lies up on the upland in a cup of stone, black and so still that the clouds in it look deeper than the clouds above. Over it stands a crag, and on the crag a cairn somebody keeps building.|The tarn is ruffled today, wind chasing cat's-paws across it, and the water's the colour of strong tea at the edge and black in the middle. The crag above is loud with wind.|{season == "winter": The tarn is frozen from shore to shore, black ice so clear you can see weed standing in it like a forest, and the crag above it is white.|The tarn on a hot day, still as glass, a dragonfly the only thing moving, the crag above it shimmering.}}
text [7b2f55] = {&山间湖躺在高地的一个石盆里，漆黑而平静，湖里的云看上去比天上的云还深。湖上方立着一座岩崖，崖顶有一堆不知谁一直在垒的石堆。|今天湖面起了皱，风在水面上追着猫爪般的涟漪，湖边的水是浓茶色，湖心是黑的。上方的岩崖风声呼啸。|{season == "winter": 山间湖从这岸冻到那岸，黑冰清得能看见水草像森林一样立在里面，上方的岩崖一片雪白。|炎热的一天，山间湖静得像玻璃，只有一只蜻蜓在动，上方的岩崖在热气里微微晃动。}}
# en: A small black mountain lake in a cup of rock under a crag, so still the sky is mirrored in it, a student sitting at the edge looking down into the water.
scene [4812cc] = 岩崖下一个石盆里的黑色小山湖，静得把天空映在水里，一个学生坐在湖边俯视水面。
# en: Climb the crag above it
opt.left.label [bf6068] = 爬上湖上方的岩崖
# en: {&You climb the crag hand over hand to the cairn at the top and put a stone on it, as everyone does. From up here the tarn is a black eye looking at the sky.|You climb into the wind and it tries to pluck you off the crag, and doesn't. At the top you shout something, and the wind takes it away over the valley.|{season == "winter": You climb the white crag with frozen fingers and stand by the cairn over the frozen tarn, the whole upland ringing with cold.|You climb the warm rock to the cairn and lie on top of the crag in the sun like a lizard.}}
opt.left.say.1 [5369cb] = {&你手脚并用爬到崖顶的石堆边，像大家一样往上面添了一块石头。从这上面看，山间湖是一只望着天空的黑眼睛。|你迎着风往上爬，风想把你从崖上摘下来，没摘成。到了崖顶你喊了句什么，风把它带过了山谷。|{season == "winter": 你用冻僵的手指爬上雪白的岩崖，站在冰封的湖上方的石堆旁，整片高地都在寒冷中作响。|你爬上温热的岩石来到石堆边，像蜥蜴一样趴在崖顶晒太阳。}}
# en: {&A hold crumbles and you slide down the crag on your front, scraping both knees. The tarn watches, perfectly still.|The wind takes you off balance on the last pitch and you come down the scree in a hurry, bruised.|{season == "winter": The ice on the crag is harder than it looks, and so is the ground at the bottom.|The rock is hot enough to burn your hands, and you let go of the wrong one.}}
opt.left.say.2 [9447c2] = {&一个抓手碎了，你肚皮朝下滑下岩崖，两个膝盖都擦破了。山间湖看着，纹丝不动。|最后一段风把你吹得失去平衡，你匆匆顺着碎石滑下来，一身瘀青。|{season == "winter": 岩崖上的冰比看上去更硬，底下的地面也是。|岩石烫得能灼手，你松错了一只手。}}
# en: Sit and look into the water
opt.right.label [6443fd] = 坐下来看着湖水
# en: {&You sit at the edge and look into the tarn until the clouds in it seem to be the real ones and the sky above a picture of them. The cold comes up out of the stone into you, and you walk down stiff.|You watch the wind write on the water and rub it out, write and rub out, for an hour, in a wind that goes straight through your coat.|{season == "winter": You lie on the black ice and look down at the weed forest standing under you, and something long and silver turns among it, and is gone. You get up shaking with cold.|You look into the still water and see yourself and the sky behind you, and behind the sky, deeper, more sky. You come down sunburnt.}}
opt.right.say.1 [f3b89d] = {&你坐在湖边望着湖水，直到湖里的云好像才是真的，天上的反倒成了它们的画像。寒气从石头里渗进你身体，下山时你浑身僵硬。|你看着风在水上写字又擦掉，写了又擦，看了一个小时，风直直穿透了你的外套。|{season == "winter": 你趴在黑冰上，看着身下那片水草森林，有个长长的银色东西在其中一转，就不见了。你爬起来时冷得直发抖。|你望着静水，看见了自己和身后的天空，天空后面，更深处，还有天空。下山时你晒伤了。}}

@event tarn_angler
# en: The Angler at the Tarn
title [c20bca] = 湖边的垂钓人
# en: An old angler is sitting on a folding stool at the tarn's edge, as he has every fine day, the shepherds tell you, for forty years. He's fishing for a trout that lives in the black middle and that nobody but him has ever seen. "She's there," he says, not looking round. "She's just choosy. Sit, if you'll sit quiet."
text [9a8f35] = 一位老垂钓人坐在湖边的折叠凳上，牧羊人们说，四十年来每个晴天他都在这儿。他钓的是一条住在漆黑湖心、除了他谁也没见过的鳟鱼。“她在那儿，”他说，头也不回，“只是挑剔。要坐就坐，安静点。”
# en: An old angler in a tweed hat sitting on a folding stool at the edge of a black mountain lake, a long rod over the water, a student sitting down beside him.
scene [8a1c36] = 一位戴粗呢帽的老垂钓人坐在黑色山湖边的折叠凳上，一根长竿伸向水面，一个学生在他身旁坐下。
# en: Sit quiet with him all day
opt.left.label [832d8e] = 安安静静陪他坐一天
# en: You sit quiet with him all day in the wind. He doesn't catch her. Near sunset the line goes taut once, hard, and slack again, and he laughs out loud. "There," he says. "Told you." It's the best thing that happens all week. You're chilled to the bone.
opt.left.say.1 [8001b0] = 你在风里安安静静陪他坐了一整天。他没钓到她。快日落时，钓线猛地绷紧了一下，又松了，他放声大笑。“看，”他说，“我说过吧。”这是这一星期里最好的一件事。你冷到了骨头里。
# en: Offer to charm the line
opt.right.label [ba97b4] = 提议给钓线施个咒
# en: You offer a little charm on the hook. He looks at you as if you'd spat in the tarn. "Then it wouldn't be her choosing," he says, and you sit in silence, the charm unspoken, and learn something about patience that no lecture covered.
opt.right.say.1 [5707e9] = 你提议在钩上施一个小咒。他看你的眼神，好像你往湖里吐了口水。“那就不是她自己选的了，”他说。你们在沉默中坐着，咒语没念出口，你学到了一种任何课上都没教过的耐心。

@event quarry_face
# en: The Quarry Face
title [831a65] = 采石场的崖壁
# en: {&The old quarry's walls are full of fossils, shells from a sea that left before the valley had a name. A frayed old rope hangs down the tallest face, left by somebody braver, and the ledges are thick with the best of the shells.|The quarry after rain: every face streaming, every fossil shining, the rope dark with wet.|{season == "winter": The quarry in a hard bright frost, the faces rimed white and the shells standing out like carvings.|The quarry in high summer, the pale faces throwing the heat back at you and the shells too hot to touch.}}
text [4202cf] = {&老采石场的石壁里满是化石，那是一片在山谷还没有名字时就退去的海留下的贝壳。最高的崖壁上垂着一根磨损的旧绳子，是某个更有胆量的人留下的，岩架上满是最好的贝壳。|雨后的采石场：每面崖壁都在淌水，每块化石都在发亮，绳子湿得发黑。|{season == "winter": 严霜下的采石场，崖壁结着白霜，贝壳像雕刻一样凸显出来。|盛夏的采石场，浅色的崖壁把热气反射到你身上，贝壳烫得摸不得。}}
# en: An old stone quarry with tall pale rock faces full of fossil shells, ledges and a rope left by climbers, a student testing a handhold.
scene [c21e2f] = 一座老采石场，高大的浅色崖壁里满是贝壳化石，岩架和一根攀岩者留下的绳子，一个学生在试一个抓手。
# en: Climb the face
opt.left.label [d88a36] = 攀上崖壁
# en: {&You climb to the top ledge on the old rope and your own fingers, and find a spiral shell as big as your hand, perfect, waiting. You climb down with it in your teeth.|You climb the wet face, slowly, every hold slick, and come down muddy and triumphant with a fossil fern.|{season == "winter": You climb the frosty face with numb fingers and find, on the top ledge, a sea-urchin turned to stone, sitting there like an egg in a nest.|You climb the hot face with chalky fingers and find, on the top ledge, a sea-urchin turned to stone, sitting there like an egg in a nest.}}
opt.left.say.1 [6b3e5c] = {&你靠着那根旧绳子和自己的手指爬到最高的岩架，找到一枚手掌大的螺旋贝壳，完好无损，正等着你。你叼着它爬了下来。|你慢慢爬上湿漉漉的崖壁，每个抓手都很滑，下来时满身是泥，却得意洋洋地带着一块蕨类化石。|{season == "winter": 你用冻麻的手指爬上结霜的崖壁，在最高的岩架上发现一个变成石头的海胆，像窝里的一颗蛋。|你用沾满白垩的手指爬上发烫的崖壁，在最高的岩架上发现一个变成石头的海胆，像窝里的一颗蛋。}}
# en: {&The old rope gives a yard of slack and you slide down the face, skinning both palms. The quarry's echo says something sarcastic.|Halfway up, a wet hold comes away in your hand. You land on the scree heap at the bottom, bruised and furious.|{season == "winter": The frost on the ledge is ice. You come down faster than you went up.|Your sweating fingers slip on the hot rock. You come down faster than you went up.}}
opt.left.say.2 [1d43a6] = {&那根旧绳子松了一码，你顺着崖壁滑下来，两只手掌都擦破了。采石场的回声说了句挖苦话。|爬到一半，一个湿抓手在你手里脱落了。你摔在底下的碎石堆上，一身瘀青，气坏了。|{season == "winter": 岩架上的霜是冰。你下来得比上去快多了。|你汗湿的手指在发烫的岩石上一滑。你下来得比上去快多了。}}
# en: Hunt the scree for fossils
opt.right.label [04df97] = 在碎石里找化石
# en: {&You turn over scree for an hour and find a dozen broken shells and one whole one, small and perfect. Your back aches from the stooping.|You sift the wet scree and find a tooth, a real tooth, from something that swam. Your hands are cold and gritty.|{season == "winter": You find nothing in the frozen scree for an hour, and then a little curled ammonite, which is enough. Your fingers have stopped working.|You find nothing in the baking scree for an hour, and then a little curled ammonite, which is enough. The back of your neck is burnt.}}
opt.right.say.1 [3372f4] = {&你翻了一个小时碎石，找到一打碎贝壳和一枚完整的，又小又完美。弯腰弯得你背疼。|你在湿碎石里筛出一颗牙，一颗真正的牙，来自某种会游泳的东西。你的手又冷又糙。|{season == "winter": 你在冻硬的碎石里一个小时什么也没找到，然后找到一枚小小的卷曲菊石，这就够了。你的手指已经不听使唤了。|你在晒烫的碎石里一个小时什么也没找到，然后找到一枚小小的卷曲菊石，这就够了。你的后颈晒伤了。}}

@event quarry_echo
# en: Back Chat
title [d658b8] = 顶嘴
# en: The valley says the quarry's echo is full of opinions, and a shepherd boy on the rim dares you to try it. "Good morning," you call. "Is it?" says the quarry. You call that you're from the academy. "Oh," says the quarry, "one of those." The shepherd boy is lying on the grass, helpless.
text [b732fc] = 山谷里的人说，采石场的回声满肚子意见，崖边一个放羊的男孩激你试试。“早上好，”你喊。“是吗？”采石场说。你喊说你是学院来的。“哦，”采石场说，“那种人啊。”放羊的男孩笑得躺倒在草地上，爬不起来。
# en: The floor of an old quarry, a student with hands cupped to their mouth shouting at a pale rock face, a shepherd boy on the rim laughing.
scene [d94eee] = 老采石场的底部，一个学生双手拢在嘴边朝浅色的崖壁大喊，崖边一个放羊的男孩在大笑。
# en: Argue with it
opt.left.label [0db69c] = 跟它吵
# en: You argue with the quarry for half an hour, about the weather, the academy and whether it has any right to an opinion. It gives as good as it gets, in your own voice, and gets the last word, every time. The boy calls it a draw. You're hoarse, and somehow lost.
opt.left.say.1 [cb7789] = 你跟采石场吵了半个钟头，吵天气，吵学院，吵它有没有资格发表意见。它用你自己的声音针锋相对，而且每次都抢到最后一句。男孩判了个平局。你嗓子哑了，不知怎么还是输了。
# en: Ask it a real question
opt.right.label [f5a488] = 问它一个正经问题
# en: You ask it what it's seen. There's a long pause, the only one all morning. "Sea," says the quarry at last, "and then not." Then it goes back to mocking your accent. You sit on the scree a long time, feeling very small and very recent.
opt.right.say.1 [4a74c8] = 你问它见过什么。一阵长长的停顿，整个上午唯一的一次。“海，”采石场终于说，“然后就没了。”接着它又开始学你的口音取笑你。你在碎石上坐了很久，觉得自己非常渺小，也非常新近。

@event quarry_millstone
# en: The Last Millstone
title [651863] = 最后一块磨盘
# en: Two old stonecutters are finishing a millstone on the quarry floor, the last, they say, this quarry will ever cut: the mill's old stone is worn smooth after forty years, and nobody young wants the trade. It has to be levered onto a sledge before the miller's cart comes. They look at you, and at your arms, and hand you a bar.
text [6536bc] = 两个老石匠正在采石场底完成一块磨盘，他们说，这是这座采石场凿的最后一块了：磨坊的旧磨盘用了四十年已经磨平，年轻人都不想干这行。磨坊主的车来之前，得把它撬上雪橇。他们看看你，又看看你的胳膊，递给你一根撬棍。
# en: A quarry floor, two old stonecutters with chisels finishing a great round millstone, a student helping lever it with a long bar.
scene [8e4a07] = 采石场底，两个拿着凿子的老石匠正在完成一块巨大的圆磨盘，一个学生帮着用长撬棍撬它。
# en: Put your back into it
opt.left.label [64580b] = 使出全身力气
# en: The three of you lever the great stone up inch by inch with bars and wedges, and when it settles on the sledge both old men sit down on it and laugh. They give you a chip of the stone to keep, "for luck at the mill". Your back will remember it for days.
opt.left.say.1 [99a5b5] = 你们三个用撬棍和楔子一寸一寸地把大石头撬起来，它落到雪橇上时，两个老人都坐在上面笑了。他们给了你一块石屑留着，“到磨坊图个吉利”。你的背好几天都会记得这件事。
# en: Float it with a spell
opt.right.label [8cee3b] = 用咒语把它浮起来
# en: The stone rises a foot off the ground, turns slowly like a coin, and settles on the sledge as gently as a cake on a plate. The stonecutters say nothing for a long time. Then the elder says, "Well, that's the trade finished, then," and shakes your hand.
opt.right.say.1 [5b9629] = 石头离地浮起一尺，像硬币一样慢慢转了一圈，轻轻落在雪橇上，就像把蛋糕放到盘子里。石匠们好久没说话。然后年长的那个说：“好吧，这门手艺算是到头了，”跟你握了握手。
# en: The stone lifts, wobbles and comes down on the bar, which springs up and catches your shin. The stonecutters lever it on the old way. They're kind about it. Your shin isn't.
opt.right.say.2 [126890] = 石头浮了起来，晃了晃，砸在撬棍上，撬棍弹起来打中了你的小腿。石匠们用老办法把它撬了上去。他们对此很宽厚。你的小腿可不。

@event drovers_long_table
# en: The Long Table
title [944a7a] = 长桌
# en: {&The Drovers' Inn has one long table, one fire and one rule, which nobody can remember. Drovers, tinkers and a man with a bear on a rope share it with whoever comes in.|Market night at the Drovers'. The long table is three to a seat, the fire roars and two drovers are arm-wrestling for the last of the stew.|A wet night at the Drovers'. Steam rises off every coat at the long table, and a tinker by the fire is singing a song with far too many verses.}
text [81cfac] = {&赶畜人客栈只有一张长桌、一个炉火和一条规矩，而谁也记不住那条规矩是什么。赶畜人、补锅匠，还有一个牵着熊的男人，跟每个进门的人同桌。|赶畜人客栈的集市之夜。长桌一个座位挤三个人，炉火熊熊，两个赶畜人在掰手腕争最后一点炖菜。|赶畜人客栈的一个雨夜。长桌边每件外套都冒着热气，炉火旁一个补锅匠在唱一首段数多得离谱的歌。}
# en: A rough country inn with one long table packed with drovers, tinkers and travellers, a big fire, tankards, a student squeezing onto the bench.
scene [b388d1] = 一家粗陋的乡村客栈，一张长桌挤满了赶畜人、补锅匠和旅人，大炉火，大酒杯，一个学生正挤上长凳。
# en: Squeeze onto the bench
opt.left.label [075ee0] = 挤上长凳
# en: {&You buy a round of the cheapest beer in the valley, which tastes of it, and in return get the whole history of the bear. The bear sleeps through it.|You pay for a bowl of stew and sit between two drovers who argue across you about the price of wethers. By the end you're arguing too.|You buy the singer a pint to wet the next verse, join the chorus by the third and lead it by the seventh.}
opt.left.say.1 [a47dac] = {&你请了一轮山谷里最便宜的啤酒，喝起来也就那个味，换来了那头熊的全部生平。熊一直在睡。|你付钱要了一碗炖菜，坐在两个赶畜人中间，他们隔着你争阉羊的价钱。到最后你也加入了争论。|你请唱歌的人喝一品脱润润下一段的嗓子，到第三段就跟着唱起了副歌，到第七段你已经在领唱了。}
# en: Arm-wrestle a drover
opt.right.label [4779e1] = 跟赶畜人掰手腕
# en: {&Elbow on the table, hand in a hand like a saddle. You hold, and hold, and put him down, and the long table roars. The bear wakes up and roars too.|You win the last of the stew, and it's terrible, and you eat every mouthful in front of the whole room.|You beat the champion of the long table and he buys you a drink, and then wants a rematch, and then another drink.}
opt.right.say.1 [2acaff] = {&手肘撑在桌上，手握进一只像马鞍一样的手里。你撑住，再撑住，把他扳倒了，整张长桌一片吼叫。熊醒了，也吼了一声。|你赢了最后的炖菜，味道糟透了，你当着满屋子人一口不剩地吃完了。|你赢了长桌的冠军，他请你喝了一杯，然后要求再比一场，然后又一杯。}
# en: {&He puts your hand down on the table like a man closing a gate. Everyone's very nice about it. Your wrist isn't.|You lose the stew and very nearly your wrist.|You lose so fast the room doesn't notice. Your shoulder does.}
opt.right.say.2 [5b3c8c] = {&他像关一扇门那样把你的手按在桌上。大家对此都很客气。你的手腕可不。|你输了炖菜，手腕也差点输掉。|你输得太快，满屋子都没注意到。你的肩膀注意到了。}

@event drovers_tinker
# en: The Tinker's Pack
title [d85e6a] = 补锅匠的包
# en: A tinker by the fire has his pack open on the hearth: pots, knives, scissors, a box of odd brass trinkets, and a sign that says MENDS ANYTHING. He's looking at the things you carry with a professional eye. "That's bent," he says, of something you hadn't noticed was. "I'll mend it. Or I'll trade you a luck for it."
text [e9050c] = 炉火边一个补锅匠把他的包在炉前摊开：锅、刀、剪子，一盒古怪的黄铜小玩意儿，还有一块写着“什么都能修”的牌子。他正用行家的眼光打量你随身带的东西。“那个弯了，”他说的是一样你都没注意到弯了的东西，“我给你修。或者，我拿一个‘好运’跟你换。”
# en: A tinker by an inn fire with his pack open on the floor, pots, knives and odd brass trinkets spread around him, holding up a bent spoon to a student.
scene [137c4a] = 客栈炉火边一个补锅匠把包摊在地上，锅、刀和古怪的黄铜小玩意儿散在周围，他举着一把弯勺子对着一个学生。
# en: Mend his pots while he talks
opt.left.label [533c7e] = 边听他讲边帮他补锅
# en: You sit by the fire and help him mend a drover's kettle, burning your fingers on the solder, while he tells you about every inn on the high road from here to the sea. He fixes your bag strap for nothing, in return. You know the high road now, by heart.
opt.left.say.1 [b5bf18] = 你坐在炉火边帮他补一个赶畜人的水壶，焊料烫了你的手指，他给你讲从这儿到海边的大路上的每一家客栈。作为回报，他免费给你修好了包带。现在你把那条大路记得滚瓜烂熟。
# en: Trade for one of his lucks
opt.right.label [23555d] = 换他一个“好运”
# en: You haggle him for a "luck", a brass horse no bigger than your thumb. It isn't magic. You check, twice. But you learn more about bargaining from the tinker's patter than from a year of market days, and you suspect he cheated you very fairly.
opt.right.say.1 [17e3da] = 你跟他讨价还价换来一个“好运”，一匹不比你拇指大的黄铜小马。它不带魔法。你检查了两遍。可你从补锅匠的那套说辞里学到的讨价还价，比赶一年集学到的还多，你怀疑他非常公道地骗了你。

@event drovers_loose_bear
# en: The Bear Gets Loose
title [ab51d5] = 熊跑出来了
# en: The man with the bear has fallen asleep by the fire, and the bear's rope has come undone, and the bear has decided to see what's in the kitchen. The long table empties onto the benches. The landlord is up on the bar with a ladle. The bear stops in the middle of the room and looks at you, because you're the only one not shouting.
text [431074] = 牵熊的男人在炉火边睡着了，熊的绳子松开了，熊决定去看看厨房里有什么。长桌上的人全都跳上了长凳。店主拿着一把长柄勺站到了吧台上。熊在屋子中间停下来看着你，因为只有你没在大喊。
# en: A rough country inn's taproom in uproar, a big brown bear loose among the tables with a broken rope trailing, drovers climbing onto benches, a student standing very still with a wand lowered.
scene [ddf2d4] = 一家粗陋乡村客栈的大堂乱成一团，一头大棕熊拖着断绳在桌子间晃荡，赶畜人们爬上长凳，一个学生垂着魔杖一动不动地站着。
# en: Talk the bear down
opt.left.label [a349ae] = 把熊安抚下来
# en: You hold out a hand and talk to it, low and steady, about nothing, the way you'd talk to a frightened horse. The bear listens, sighs like a bellows and sits down. You walk it back to its sleeping owner by the broken rope. The Drovers' Inn will tell this story for years.
opt.left.say.1 [6c3944] = 你伸出一只手，低声平稳地跟它说话，什么都说，就像跟一匹受惊的马说话那样。熊听着，像风箱一样叹了口气，坐了下来。你牵着断绳把它送回它熟睡的主人身边。赶畜人客栈会把这件事讲上好多年。
# en: The bear listens to about half of what you say, then shoves past you towards the kitchen, and you go over a bench backwards. It finds the cheese. The owner wakes up and fetches it out by the ear, apologising to everyone, especially you.
opt.left.say.2 [dd9907] = 熊只听了你一半的话，就把你推开朝厨房去了，你仰面翻过了一张长凳。它找到了奶酪。主人醒了，揪着耳朵把它拽了出来，向每个人道歉，尤其是你。
# en: Lure it out with the stew pot
opt.right.label [3dc585] = 用炖菜锅把它引出去
# en: You buy the rest of the stew, all of it, and carry the steaming pot out into the yard, and the bear follows you like a dog. It eats the lot under the stars while the drovers cheer from the doorway. You smell of mutton for two days.
opt.right.say.1 [77fccf] = 你把剩下的炖菜全买了下来，端着冒热气的锅走到院子里，熊像狗一样跟着你。它在星空下把一锅吃了个精光，赶畜人们在门口欢呼。你身上的羊肉味两天都没散。
